  "title": "Time, days & months",
  "goal": "Ask and tell the time, name the days of the week and months, and talk about when things happen.",
  "intro": "Time in Malayalam is counted with **മണി** *maṇi* (literally 'bell'): മൂന്ന് മണി 'three o'clock'. Fractions are built in: **-അര** 'half past', **-ഏകാൽ** 'quarter past', **-ഏമുക്കാൽ** 'three quarters past'.\n\nThe days of the week are named after the planets (as in many languages) and end in **-ആഴ്ച** (*-āḻcha*, 'week'): തിങ്കളാഴ്ച 'Monday'. For months, people normally use the English names (ജനുവരി, ഫെബ്രുവരി…); the traditional Malayalam calendar months are used for festivals and astrology.",
